WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:07.170
Now hitting, number 1: Jeff Keene!

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.230
Play!

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:13.150
We didn't get three runs just by luck or coincidence...

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.990
Murdoch took that hit.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.750
Robinson made that tackle to save a double play...

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:27.380
And Nelson's persistence triggered Silva's bad throw.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.970
Watts left us with the attitude to never give up, which gave us

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.220
this counter attack!

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:50.250
It's out of here!

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.690
Keene gets a three-run home run in the bottom of the seventh, and the game's 8-6!

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.400
Yeah!

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.180
The Hornets have closed the gap to a mere two runs!

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.180
This game is still far from over!

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.660
Just two runs!

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:03.860
Nice, Keene!

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.750
And it looks like the Hornets are bringing out a new pitcher.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:18.570
Attention, please. Pitcher, number 56:

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:24.000
Goro Shigeno!

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:32.940
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:32.940
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:38.240
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:38.240
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.620
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.620
the only thing I truly have

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.910
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.910
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:54.250
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:54.250
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:59.510
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:59.510
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:04.890
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:04.890
I had begun to understand many things

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:10.980
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:10.980
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:16.530
garakuta no yama kara

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:16.530
In the junk I've piled up,

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.610
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.610
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:25.910
hibike kono koe yo

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:25.910
Let my voice echo on.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:32.210
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:32.210
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:37.840
namida kareru made

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:37.840
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.890
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.890
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:48.220
namida hareru made

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:48.220
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:53.230
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:53.230
though I may lose my way,

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:57.070
egakikake no ima

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:57.070
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.570
kizamu

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:04.320
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:59.860
akashi

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.320
kono te de

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:10.080
Final Chance

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:10.080
Final Chance

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.410
Darling!

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.840
I'm your darling!

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.060
What are you doing?!

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.100
I was just about to kiss him!

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:26.430
At the top of the eighth, the Coyotes are back to the top of their order.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:32.520
The Hornets are leaving their fate to the 19-year-old Shigeno, hoping he'll hold down the fort.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.940
Good luck, Honda.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.860
Now hitting, number 1: Strawberry!

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:50.020
However, if you feel any pain or numbness during practices or games,

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:53.180
you are to stop pitching immediately and come see me.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.750
Under those conditions, I'll help you.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:02.300
I don't know when my arm will start to hurt...

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.880
Play!

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:07.010
...but we don't have many pitchers left.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.540
Just two innings.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.210
I'll put my faith in my batters, and hold them down as best as I can!

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.480
What are you doing, Shigeno?!

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:21.230
He... got hit right off the bat.{lol, pun}

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:25.360
Damn!

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.250
Ball!

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.400
92 mph?

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.710
Hey, that's not very fast.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:47.680
His pitches weren't exactly fast in the warm-up either.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.310
I thought he'd rev his engine up on the mound, but...

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.180
Ball!

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:57.830
Ball!

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.790
Ball four!

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.640
No outs, bases loaded...

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.530
That's really bad...

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.490
We were about to make a comeback!

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.710
What are you doing, putting yourselves against a wall?!

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:17.580
Now hitting, number 5: Silva!

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:23.930
We only have Gazzara, a rookie, and Sullivan, who can only pitch once.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.010
Hold it here somehow, Shigeno.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.810
This is bad...

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.100
I can't pitch like I want to...

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:37.020
I didn't practice enough because of my arm, and it's come back to bite me.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.110
Ball!

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:48.910
Ball!

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:51.590
Are you stupid?!

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:53.450
Just throw it down the middle!

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:58.190
Looks like you're not quite ready yet.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.630
I'm gonna slam your ball right here, pal.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:03.710
I gotta hold him down no matter what!

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:07.470
Watch out!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:15.970
What?!

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.140
Out!

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:18.230
Out!

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:20.730
Out!

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.990
T-Triple play...

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:27.820
Lucky us...

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:30.990
W-We somehow got out of it.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.880
That's Shigeno for you.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:44.040
A normal pitcher would've dodged that or taken it in the face.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:44.800
Yeah...

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:49.410
But I'm a little worried about his pitching.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.760
We're in luck!

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.640
The game is still flowing in our favor!

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.630
We can turn this around!

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:57.140
You got a moment, Shigeno?

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.060
Oh?

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.340
Yeah.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.410
What do you need?

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.570
Did I miss a sign or something?

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.220
This is just an assumption,

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:12.620
but are you having circulatory problems?

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:20.250
I saw you worrying about your hand in that one game and found it odd.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.380
You shook your hand to warm it up.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.590
That's what people do when their blood isn't flowing.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.710
Circulatory problems?

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.060
What are you talking about?

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:32.610
It was a little cold that day, that's all.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.760
Don't play dumb with me.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:39.090
With today's pitching, and how you've been practicing,

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.180
I can see right through you.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:48.960
I guess I can't fool a catcher who always watches the pitchers.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:53.030
Yeah, I do have a circulatory problem.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:58.040
I got it checked out at a hospital, and I'm managing the symptoms with drugs.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:01.550
But there's nothing to worry about.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:06.040
I don't feel any pain, and I plan to have surgery done after this game.

00:08:06.530 --> 00:08:09.660
I couldn't throw well last inning because I wasn't fully warmed up.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.950
I'll definitely hold them down in the next inning.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.410
That's not how it works.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.090
What?

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:18.930
I can't approve of a guy who hides his injury and puts the team at risk!

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:21.980
Especially in a game with this much riding on it!

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.270
That's not how professionals work!

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:25.220
Switch out.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:28.020
If you won't, I'll tell the coach and make you switch out.

00:08:29.060 --> 00:08:31.690
Switch... out?

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.270
That's right.

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:36.860
You're just being selfish, playing for your own satisfaction.

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:39.840
You kept your injury a secret to play in the playoff game?

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:41.080
Over my dead body.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:42.870
Hold on.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.810
I'm sorry for hiding the injury,

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:51.180
but Watts did his best with his injury,

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.760
and you defended him!

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.550
Why are you criticizing me?

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.190
Because you and him are different.

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:02.140
He was allowed to play with both the team trainer and the team doctor knowing about his condition.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:07.480
You don't know when your blood circulation could stop,

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.950
yet you're trying to play in the game, keeping that condition a secret.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:12.030
You're so much worse!

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:16.460
I wouldn't play if I felt that I couldn't!

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:17.400
But...

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:20.640
I know that we don't have many pitchers to spare,

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:23.580
so I can't just tell everyone that I'm injured!

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:27.500
I'll definitely hold down the next inning!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:31.520
Why can't I go out on the mound for our team's victory?!

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.020
Then the next inning.

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:41.220
If you allow a single runner on, you're done.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:44.850
I'm not letting you play otherwise.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:45.660
Got it?

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.140
Out!

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:03.710
Nice job!

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:06.350
Good, we can get a run with a single.

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:08.000
Let's see it, Robinson!

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:16.610
Out!

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:17.380
Nice.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:19.440
That was so close!

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:21.300
We almost got a run!

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:32.440
Oh, Shigeno's still playing?

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:33.820
Yeah.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.820
The Hornets probably don't have many pitchers left.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.840
I wonder if he'll be okay.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:41.430
He doesn't seem to be doing so well today.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:43.740
Play!

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:48.390
If you allow a single runner on, you're done.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:50.630
I'm not letting you play otherwise.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:51.460
Got it?

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:56.910
Strike!

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.100
Strike two!

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:08.980
Strike out!

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:12.470
He's finally got his game on!

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:14.690
That's what we wanted to see from the start!

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.200
Geez...

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.860
He sure had us worried.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:21.360
Strike out!

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:23.450
Yeah!

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:28.230
You're just being selfish, playing for your own satisfaction.

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:31.170
You kept your injury a secret to play in the playoff game?

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:32.710
Over my dead body.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:35.330
Damn.

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:36.630
I hate to admit it,

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:39.300
but Keene's right.

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:46.840
I never thought I'd put the team at risk by playing with an injury.

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:48.220
Damn it!

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:51.190
Strike out!

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:13.870
We've nearly reached the end of the playoff game for the Northern League's Central Division.

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:20.300
The Hornets make their final attack in the bottom of the ninth with the Coyotes leading 8 to 6.

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:24.120
Oh, we've just received word

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:29.080
that the Boston Axe-Knights in the Western Division made a comeback win after ten innings!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:29.720
What?!

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:33.390
They've been selected for the Northern League's wild card spot.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.950
Hey, what's a wild card?

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:42.860
It's a second place team with the most amount of wins in the league.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.660
It's like a consolation position.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:51.280
So... the Hornets have to win if they want to get to the next stage?

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:52.000
Yeah.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:03.720
Looks like we'll have to make a comeback now.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:07.640
But you know, we're up against Springer, their closer.

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:11.650
He's made 48 saves this season, the most in the league.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:16.930
True, it's gonna be hard to get runs off him.

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:18.270
Listen up.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:23.340
You've all done well, making it this far.

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:28.450
We've always ranked low, being called the delinquents of the Northern League,

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:35.120
so I had never thought that we'd still be playing games that could excite the fans.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.300
Look at that.

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:43.800
We have many fans who believed in our victory even when we were down by eight runs.

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:50.600
We've still got three outs to work with.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:53.350
We shouldn't be giving up here.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:58.510
Let's win in front of our fans and make it through to the next round.

00:13:58.510 --> 00:13:59.520
Yeah!

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:03.250
Now hitting, number 2: Roy!

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:05.830
Just three more outs.

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:07.070
With Springer pitching,

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:09.180
even a miracle won't get you two runs.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.410
Strike!

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:14.790
That's fast.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.250
Shigeno.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:24.450
It looks like I was a bit hard on you earlier.

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:28.180
Strike!

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:33.610
There are lots of guys who play through injuries or illness.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.640
The longer your professional career,

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:40.770
the more likely it'll be for you to have an injury.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.830
But we're still young.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:47.190
You shouldn't force yourself here.

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.030
You have talent.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:55.330
The Hornets have definitely gotten stronger.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:59.740
Even if we can't win this year, if we play without any major injuries,

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:05.890
we'll have chances to win the league, or even to play in the World Series.

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:06.920
Ball!

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:13.350
In order to do that, I can't have you retire right now,

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:15.320
as you will be the leader of the Hornets' pitchers.

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.450
I'm not concerned about you,

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:23.060
this is simply what I think will keep the Hornets strong.

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:33.990
Safe! Safe!

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:35.370
All right!

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.790
Yeah!

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:43.130
Hey, Keene!

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:47.300
Thanks for the warning,

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:51.630
but I have a disease where I can't think about the future.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:58.180
Plus, a guy who can't do what needs to be done today definitely can't do it tomorrow.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:03.900
Now hitting, number 3: Nelson!

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:07.570
I definitely can't screw up here.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:11.360
Shoot!

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:14.660
Out!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:15.530
Damn it!

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:20.450
Now hitting, number 1: Jeff Keene!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.970
A home run will tie it up.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:25.110
A double-play will end the game.

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:26.850
It all comes down to this!

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.130
It's all in your hands, Keene!

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:38.970
Strike!

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.420
That's one strike.

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:44.230
Stop sighing and cheer him on!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.810
Watts!

00:16:46.810 --> 00:16:49.180
Wh-What are you doing?

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.500
Shouldn't you be in the hospital?

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:52.950
Well, sort of.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:54.910
I got a quick check-up,

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:59.580
but I wanted to be with everyone, whether we win or lose.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:05.330
Strike two!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.000
Get a hit, Keene!

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.420
That idiot!

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:16.180
A guy who can't do what needs to be done today definitely can't do it tomorrow.

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:18.220
I...

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:22.930
wasn't talking about that!

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:26.440
Wait!

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:27.810
Don't touch that ball!

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:32.360
Yeah, that's a hit!

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:34.280
No.

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:37.820
Foul! Foul!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.320
Wh-What?!

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:40.490
How can that be?

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:46.010
If the ball bounces off the pitcher's plate and then past the foul line, it's a foul.

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:47.760
That's right.

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:51.960
The plate is treated like a rock, not like a base.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:56.900
So it made an irregular bounce out of bounds.

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:58.690
Damn it, just our luck!

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:00.970
Not even an inch higher, and it would've been in the outfields.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:07.060
Yeah, and after a good hit like that, something bad usually happens...

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.240
Shields! Catch it!

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:18.910
Keep running!

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:20.570
Hurry! Throw it home!

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:29.370
Out!

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:30.540
All right!

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.980
Oh my god!

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.610
Time out! Time out!

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:38.800
That was a home run!

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:40.490
Check the video!

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:41.640
It hit the foul post!

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:45.560
Even if the glove touches it, it's still a home run if it hits the post!

00:18:45.990 --> 00:18:51.040
It looks like Coach Stacy is arguing about how the hit was treated.

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:52.730
Let's check the video.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:00.840
That's very close.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:03.370
It does look like it hit the post!

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.580
Damn it!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.200
Are you blind?!

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.200
It only hit the post!

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.250
That's a home run, you idiot!

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:18.880
Coach, the video doesn't clearly show whether the ball hit the post.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.810
If it were obvious, we'd understand,

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:29.280
but it's unclear, so the ruling on the field stands.

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:31.270
Th-Then, check the post.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:33.900
There'd be a mark if the ball hit!

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:36.880
We can't use that as evidence.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:40.950
Even if there's a mark, we can't be sure it's from today.

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:44.370
I'm sorry, but that's how it is.

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:47.290
It didn't go through...

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:52.710
Seeing how Keene's first hit ended up, it seems the Goddess of Victory isn't on your side.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.240
Umpire, a new ball!

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:01.390
A ball!

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:03.130
Umpire, check the ball!

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:04.610
Huh?

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:20.840
Home run!

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:25.820
The judgment has been overturned, and Keene's hit has been confirmed as a home run!

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:27.160
It's a tie game!

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:29.600
All right!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.670
Yes! It's a tie!

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.080
Are you serious?!

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:40.670
Looks like they're arguing now.

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:42.010
Well, of course.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:47.800
But with something so obvious, they have to approve the home run.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:51.590
Yeah, but I'm surprised you noticed that, Shigeno.

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:55.350
But now that I think about it, I messed up.

00:20:55.930 --> 00:21:00.280
If we go into extra innings with a tie game, I have to keep pitching.

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:08.180
We're still tied!

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:10.140
We haven't lost yet!

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:12.490
We'll get runs in the tenth inning,

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:15.370
so it's up to you to hold them down right here.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:16.090
Yeah.

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:21.780
Now hitting, number 11: Parker!

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.260
Yes, it went through!

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:33.250
Now hitting, number 33: Murdoch!

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:36.600
If I hit a home run here, we'll win!

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:39.360
Then I'd be today's...

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.460
Man of the Day!

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:45.650
Out!

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:47.490
Out!

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.160
Damn it!

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:54.980
The game between the Hornets and the Coyotes is tied after nine innings,

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:57.580
and they're heading into extra innings now.

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:03.170
Can you play, Shigeno?

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:05.930
Of course.

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:10.370
In fact, I'm finally feeling warmed up after pitching for two innings.

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:19.230
You might end up pitching for a while.

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:24.480
Are you going to stay quiet about your condition until you give up a hit or your arm starts hurting?

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:28.170
Enough with that talk, Keene.

00:22:28.170 --> 00:22:32.700
I'm going to do my job without complaint so long as I'm here.

00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:37.630
Play!

00:22:46.130 --> 00:22:51.630
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:46.130 --> 00:22:51.630
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:58.350
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:58.350
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:00.020
yume wo

00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:03.190
You were chasing your dream.

00:23:00.890 --> 00:23:03.190
oikaketeiru

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:05.980
ground no ue ni

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.190
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:09.190
ochiru ase ga

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:13.160
mabushikatta yo

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:13.160
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:20.580
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:20.580
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:27.880
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:27.880
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:32.630
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:35.650
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:35.650
onaji ashi ato

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:38.260
zutto mae kara

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:43.310
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:40.020
kizukazu ni

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:43.310
suki ni natta

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:45.600
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:50.440
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:50.440
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:53.030
zutto mae kara

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:58.120
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:54.910
otagai ni

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:58.120
hikareteita

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:00.330
kono kimochi wa

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:07.330
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:24:00.330 --> 00:24:07.330
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:15.450
Preview

00:24:10.090 --> 00:24:15.450
Preview

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:14.970
I'll play extra innings! Screw my arm!

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:19.600
After multiple strikeouts, we're one step away from breaking the tie-game record.

00:24:20.010 --> 00:24:21.100
Then...

00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:25.100
Next time, on Major: Break the Limit.

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:27.540
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:31.160
Next Time

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:31.160
Next Time

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:31.160
Break the Limit

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:31.160
Break the Limit
